Dialogue: 2,0:00:00.20,0:00:49.92,Hook,,0,0,0,,{\an8\pos(540,54)\fad(200,0)\fnRoundHog SemiBold\fs34\c&H001CCEFF}Alex Jung (Unikraft)
Dialogue: 2,0:00:00.20,0:00:49.92,Hook,,0,0,0,,{\an8\pos(540,118)\fad(200,0)}“Issues are worth more than
Dialogue: 2,0:00:00.20,0:00:49.92,Hook,,0,0,0,,{\an8\pos(540,190)\fad(200,0)}pull requests”
Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.10,0:00:01.04,Caption,,0,0,0,,I think definitely the
Dialogue: 0,0:00:01.04,0:00:01.86,Caption,,0,0,0,,most valuable thing we
Dialogue: 0,0:00:01.86,0:00:03.28,Caption,,0,0,0,,can get from open source
Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.28,0:00:04.80,Caption,,0,0,0,,is issues more than pull
Dialogue: 0,0:00:04.80,0:00:05.15,Caption,,0,0,0,,requests.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.14,0:00:06.14,Caption,,0,0,0,,I think this has been
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.14,0:00:07.32,Caption,,0,0,0,,true even before AI.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.32,0:00:08.76,Caption,,0,0,0,,There was a book on
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.76,0:00:09.92,Caption,,0,0,0,,building in the open
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.92,0:00:10.90,Caption,,0,0,0,,it's one of the Stripe
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.90,0:00:11.76,Caption,,0,0,0,,Press books
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.76,0:00:12.90,Caption,,0,0,0,,and it shows a power
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.90,0:00:14.02,Caption,,0,0,0,,curve in terms of
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.02,0:00:14.70,Caption,,0,0,0,,contributors to any open
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.70,0:00:16.05,Caption,,0,0,0,,source project.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.05,0:00:18.16,Caption,,0,0,0,,Even recently the
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.16,0:00:20.24,Caption,,0,0,0,,creator of OpenClaw was
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.24,0:00:21.02,Caption,,0,0,0,,telling me they don't
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.02,0:00:21.94,Caption,,0,0,0,,actually accept pull
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.94,0:00:23.12,Caption,,0,0,0,,requests anymore.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.28,0:00:24.36,Caption,,0,0,0,,They just accept issues
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.36,0:00:26.10,Caption,,0,0,0,,because an issue is a
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.10,0:00:27.44,Caption,,0,0,0,,prompt basically to fix
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.44,0:00:28.12,Caption,,0,0,0,,something.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.14,0:00:29.08,Caption,,0,0,0,,And that's a user
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.08,0:00:29.52,Caption,,0,0,0,,actually going through
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.52,0:00:30.46,Caption,,0,0,0,,the effort of typing out
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.46,0:00:32.09,Caption,,0,0,0,,what they run into.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.09,0:00:33.07,Caption,,0,0,0,,If you think about where
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.07,0:00:33.65,Caption,,0,0,0,,we're going
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.65,0:00:34.63,Caption,,0,0,0,,we're building software
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.63,0:00:35.88,Caption,,0,0,0,,factories.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.94,0:00:37.48,Caption,,0,0,0,,We trust more the
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.48,0:00:38.34,Caption,,0,0,0,,factory that we've built
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.34,0:00:39.20,Caption,,0,0,0,,and all the rules that
Dialogue: 0,0:00:39.20,0:00:40.02,Caption,,0,0,0,,we've applied
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.02,0:00:41.12,Caption,,0,0,0,,rather than some random
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.12,0:00:41.80,Caption,,0,0,0,,person that's coming
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.80,0:00:42.54,Caption,,0,0,0,,along and just
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.54,0:00:42.92,Caption,,0,0,0,,I don't know
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.92,0:00:44.46,Caption,,0,0,0,,vibe coding a solution.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:44.46,0:00:45.80,Caption,,0,0,0,,It's much harder to know
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.80,0:00:47.02,Caption,,0,0,0,,whether that's correct
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.02,0:00:48.14,Caption,,0,0,0,,even if you might have
Dialogue: 0,0:00:48.14,0:00:49.89,Caption,,0,0,0,,substantial tests.
